===Etymology 3===
Declined from {{m|la|is}}. Sometimes it stands as if for ''eō tempore/locō'' ("in that time/place"), sometimes as if for ''eō modō'' ("that way"). Compare {{m|la|eā}}.

====Adverb====
{{la-adv|eō|-}}

# {{lb|la|with abl. or loc.}} [[there]], in that [[place]]
# {{lb|la|with abl. or [[quod#Latin|quod]]}} [[therefore]], [[because]], for that [[reason]]
# {{lb|la|with [[quo#Latin|quo]], of quantity}} [[so much]], to [[such]] a [[degree]]. (= {{m|la|tantō}}...{{m|la|quantō}})
#* {{Q|la|Caesar|Commentarii de Bello Gallico|VII|18|quote=usque '''eo''' ut complures dies frumento milites caruerint|t='''to such a degree''' that for several days the soldiers were without wheat}}
# {{lb|la|with dative, of motion}} [[to]] that place, [[thither]]
#* {{Q|la|Caesar|Commentarii de Bello Gallico|VII|18|quote=Caesar cognovit Vercingetorigem [...] cum equitatu [[expeditus#Noun|expeditisque]] [...] insidiarum causa '''eo''' profectum|t=Caesar learned that [[w:Vercingetorix|Vercingetorix]] with a cavalry and light armed infantry had departed '''to that place''' to perform an ambush}}
# {{lb|la|with dative, of tendency}} [[to that end]], with that [[purpose]]
# {{lb|la|with dative, of time}} [[until]], [[so long]], [[up to]] that [[time]]

